      "extract": "Let $K$ be a knot and $J_N(K;t)$ be the colored Jones polynomial of $K$ in the three-sphere $S^3$ corresponding to the $N$-dimensional representation of $sl_2(\\mathbb{C})$ (see for example [@Kirby/Melvin:INVEM91]). We normalize it so that $J_N(\\text{unknot};t)=1$. In [@Kashaev:LETMP97], R. Kashaev introduced a series of numerical link invariants and proposed a conjecture that a limit of his invariants would",
